title: Grid walking
intro: Grid movers sent somewhere walk there by themselves: to the nearest free cell, round walls and each other, giving way in a narrow aisle.
project: Empty | Grid Walkers

chapter: A floor to walk on | A tilemap with a wall across it
create: Tilemap
rename: Floor
set: Tilemap.Tiles = 111111111111\n1....1.....1\n1....1.....1\n1..........1\n111111111111
select: Main Camera
set: Transform.Position.X = 6
set: Transform.Position.Y = -2.5
look: 6, -2.5, 4
say: Here's a floor painted on a tilemap, with a wall part of the way down the middle.
deselect
create: Grid Player
rename: Worker
set: Transform.Position.X = 1.5
set: Transform.Position.Y = -1.5
set: GridMovement.Controllable = false
deselect
create: Grid Player
rename: Visitor
set: Transform.Position.X = 9.5
set: Transform.Position.Y = -3.5
set: GridMovement.Controllable = false
say: Two grid movers: a worker in the top left, and a visitor standing in the bottom right. Neither takes the keys.

chapter: Sent somewhere | Destination, and the nearest free cell
select: Worker
explain: field:GridMovement.Destination | Destination | A Grid Movement's Destination sends it walking. It takes cells, column then row, or an entity's name.
set: GridMovement.Destination = 9 1; 9 3
say: Two cells on the far side: the bottom one is nearer, but the visitor is standing in it, so the worker heads for the top one.
play
wait: 1
explain: game | Round the wall | It finds the shortest way round the wall, a cell at a time, and plans again at every cell as things move.
wait: 2
expectat: Worker = 9.5, -1.5
say: There. It empties its Destination and says it has arrived, with an Arrived event and an Arrived Message for triggers.
stop

chapter: Two in an aisle | Waiting, and giving way
select: Floor
set: Tilemap.Tiles = 1111111111\n1........1\n11111.1111\n1111111111
look: 5, -2, 3
say: Now a one-cell aisle, with a nook halfway along.
select: Worker
set: Transform.Position.X = 1.5
set: Transform.Position.Y = -1.5
set: GridMovement.Destination = 8 1
select: Visitor
set: Transform.Position.X = 8.5
set: Transform.Position.Y = -1.5
set: GridMovement.Destination = 1 1
say: The worker walks to the right end, and the visitor to the left: they'll meet in the middle.
explain: field:GridMovement.GiveWay | Give Way | Face to face, each waits this long, then one steps aside to a free cell off the other's way.
play
wait: 1.5
explain: game | Stepping aside | The visitor ducks into the nook, lets the worker by, and carries on.
wait: 3
expectat: Worker = 8.5, -1.5
expectat: Visitor = 1.5, -1.5
stop
say: That's grid walking. Blocking Layers choose which colliders are in the way, the Blocked event says when one has to wait, and scripts call Walk To, or ask a tilemap for the cells of a way with Find Steps.
